From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shayne Legault <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:34:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: apple-sftl: add verified append writes and fresh replay

Append complete data pages in fully checked blank VFL blocks while
retaining Apple's shared map, saved contexts and bootstrap members. Use
native metadata and completed-block summaries, and recover a complete
data prefix when summary completion is interrupted. Stop at ENOSPC
without erasing or reclaiming blocks.

Add block-sector read-modify-write with four-page grouping, synchronous
flush/FUA completion and a default-false logical write_enable policy.
MTD_APPLE_SFTL_WRITE also defaults off and requires H2FMI_WRITE, so the
manual read-only qualification path remains fenced. Preserve the bounded
provider policy when forwarding optional programs.

Keep the current contiguous replay contract: refuse append before any
program when the allocation floor exceeds the last replayed record.
The saved measured 64 GB map has equal floor/journal sequence 187831212.

Generate synthetic media, program them, and load a fresh map for open,
closed, interrupted and uncertain writes. Cover all 16 lanes and maximum
footer size, including VFL reservations and sequence overflow. Host
sanitizers pass 26 cases with writes enabled and 13 in read-only mode.
Hardware qualification remains separate from these tests.

Assisted-by: LLM
